  "changed_since_previous": "Rather than making `BufferedWriter::flush()` catch exceptions and return a boolean, `flush()` continues to throw; `BlockManager` catches `std::runtime_error` during block and undo writes and triggers fatal node shutdown rather than relying on `Assert()`.",
  "card": "Handles block and undo write errors explicitly so that filesystem failures (such as running out of disk space) trigger a clean fatal shutdown with diagnostic logs instead of crashing via std::terminate. In BufferedWriter, pending bytes are cleared before writing to prevent destructor retries during exception unwinding, and an Assume check detects unflushed buffers on destruction. This fixes a regression from #31551 observed when running out of disk space during benchmarks.",
